{"EmbeddableHost runs sub! on self.host in before_validation without guarding nil, so a missing host raises NoMethodError instead of producing a validation error": 0.9427200555801392, "Admin::EmbeddableHostsController update/destroy does not handle a missing record (where(...).first can return nil) and then calls methods on nil, returning 500 instead of 404": 0.895423173904419, "Migration assumes embed_category row exists and indexes [0] on an empty SQL result when the legacy embed_category setting isn't set, causing the migration to raise and abort deploy/boot before the fallback to uncategorized can be reached": 0.9230456948280334, "Host strings are interpolated directly into INSERT SQL statement without escaping, so a host containing quotes can break the migration or be interpreted as additional SQL": 0.9560615420341492, "After saving an embeddable host, the UI sets host.category using the pre-save categoryId rather than the server-persisted category_id, causing client/server state mismatch when server defaults a blank category to uncategorized": 0.8045080900192261, "The embeddable-host component does not catch errors from destroyRecord(), so a failed delete results in no user-visible error and an unhandled promise rejection": 0.9486586451530457}